2. Native Media Runtime (mpv & FFmpeg)
--------------------------------------

Konata uses pinned, SHA-256-verified builds of mpv 0.42.0 and FFmpeg 9.0.2
tracked by native/konata-native/*-manifest.json and distributed via the
dedicated companion repository https://github.com/ClainSt/Konata-Native
(fetched locally via `dart run tool/fetch_native.dart`):
- Windows x64 (libmpv-2.dll): built from mpv 0.42.0 (-Dgpl=false) with
  statically linked FFmpeg 9.0.2 (--enable-version3, LGPL-3.0-or-later) and
  permissive/LGPL dependencies (LuaJIT, mujs, libplacebo, libass, dav1d,
  harfbuzz, freetype, fribidi, libsoxr, libzimg, libbluray, libarchive,
  uchardet, shaderc, spirv-cross, etc.). Note that native/konata-native/windows/LICENSE.LGPL
  retains the upstream mpv artifact LGPL-2.1 file tracked by windows-manifest.json;
  the effective license of the combined Windows DLL is LGPL-3.0-or-later.
- Android ARM64 (libmpv.so & libav*.so): built from mpv-android (mpv 0.42.0 +
  FFmpeg 9.0.2 with --enable-gpl --enable-version3, GPL-3.0-or-later), plus
  libmediakitandroidhelper.so from media-kit v1.1.7 (MIT) and Android NDK
  libc++_shared.so (Apache-2.0 with LLVM Exception).
- Complete build scripts, pinned source URLs/checksums, and all Konata patches
  (dovi-hlg-fallback.patch, android-hdr.patch, windows-*.patch) are maintained
  in https://github.com/ClainSt/Konata-Native in compliance with
  GPL-3.0-or-later / LGPL-3.0-or-later.

